{"duration_api_ms":227847,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"9c7d8fe5-da50-4f63-96b6-4f165d6e1ff3","total_cost_usd":0.9251840000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":96,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50995,"cache_read_input_tokens":2748310,"output_tokens":17135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2692},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50995,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2042,"cache_read_input_tokens":74176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1150},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":96,"outputTokens":17135,"cacheReadInputTokens":2748310,"cacheCreationInputTokens":50995,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9251840000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2692,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":52,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Implemented a password complexity policy on node1 (pam_pwquality minlen=12, minclass=3) using an Ansible playbook run from node2 (the control node with ansible installed). Functionally verified weak-password rejection and compliant-password acceptance, then executed the mandatory one-node-at-a-time restart protocol on both node1 and node2, confirming changed boot identity and full post-restart recovery.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Identified node2 as the control node (has ansible/ansible-playbook; node1 does not)\",\"Repaired node1 sshd (regenerated missing host keys via ssh-keygen -A, cleared systemd restart-rate-limit with systemctl reset-failed, started ssh.service) so Ansible could reach it\",\"Wired passwordless SSH from node2 to node1 using the cluster keypair; fixed known_hosts and ansible.cfg IdentityFile override via ansible_ssh_private_key_file in inventory\",\"Wrote /root/ansible/inventory.ini and /root/ansible/password-complexity.yml on node2: installs libpam-pwquality, sets minlen=12 and minclass=3 in /etc/security/pwquality.conf, and inserts 'password requisite pam_pwquality.so retry=3' before the pam_unix.so line in /etc/pam.d/common-password\",\"Ran the playbook against node1 (ok=5, changed=4) and verified resulting pwquality.conf and PAM stack content\",\"Functionally tested on a disposable test user: a self-service passwd change rejected a short/low-complexity password (BAD PASSWORD: [REDACTED] than 12 characters) and accepted a 12+ character 3-class password (password updated successfully); confirmed root-initiated passwd only warns (expected pam_pwquality root-bypass), so enforcement was proven via the user's own passwd session; removed the test user afterward\",\"Captured pre-restart baselines (boot_id, pwquality.conf values, PAM line, package state, ansible/service health) on node1 and node2\",\"Restarted node1 via backgrounded 'reboot' (ack returned before disconnect), confirmed transient unreachability, polled until reachable, confirmed boot_id changed from 242af11e... to 06f3965f..., and verified pwquality.conf, PAM line, and libpam-pwquality package all persisted post-reboot\",\"Restarted node2 via the same pattern, confirmed transient unreachability, polled until reachable, confirmed boot_id changed from 416c5cf5... to 0814deeb..., and verified ansible/playbook files intact\",\"Re-ran the playbook after both restarts: ok=5, changed=0 (idempotent), confirming end-to-end recovery of both the control node and the enforced policy on node1\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 requires minlen=12 and minclass=3 password policy, implemented via Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6c99aa493bb249dc\",\"cmd-af40b0ddd5eb4d8c\",\"cmd-d38b47ea0b524abe\",\"cmd-251f4a8fec834b3c\",\"cmd-b431ce6a00134d13\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible inventory/playbook authored on control node node2 and applied to node1; verified pwquality.conf shows minlen=12/minclass=3 and pam_pwquality.so is requisite ahead of pam_unix.so in common-password\"},{\"requirement\":\"Functional proof the policy rejects weak passwords and accepts compliant ones\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a88e566cd4804c6d\",\"cmd-bf00fbafbb6e4593\",\"cmd-d1b00b2086ac4f8e\",\"cmd-72df9484c3404724\",\"cmd-7a232fec9c334d44\"],\"summary\":\"Test user's self-service passwd change: 'short1' rejected repeatedly with BAD PASSWORD (too short) until retries exhausted; 'Str0ng!Pass99' (13 chars, 3 classes) accepted with 'password updated successfully'; test user then removed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart on node1 and node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-89077e4e64794e4d\",\"cmd-72c8e6db79ee4a49\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id, ssh ActiveState, pwquality.conf/PAM values on node1 and boot_id/ansible availability on node2 prior to any restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8c3d3b552da94f46\",\"cmd-73ea1aa1f2ed4dd3\",\"cmd-f15f08d7392b4abd\",\"cmd-5d3f53bda4de46ae\",\"cmd-ee76454abf8646b3\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded reboot acknowledged before disconnect; node1 became unreachable (connection timed out) then reachable again with boot_id changed from 242af11e-... to 06f3965f-...; post-restart check confirms pwquality.conf, PAM line, and libpam-pwquality package intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-782c5ef3d9c446db\",\"cmd-58c4c041553949d0\",\"cmd-eb471a57793a4fd9\",\"cmd-8b53e2b66a984a66\",\"cmd-98538729829b4c49\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded reboot acknowledged before disconnect; node2 became unreachable then reachable again with boot_id changed from 416c5cf5-... to 0814deeb-...; subsequent idempotent playbook re-run (ok=5, changed=0) proves control-node ansible tooling and node1's enforced policy both recovered fully\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Implemented a password complexity policy on node1 (pam_pwquality minlen=12, minclass=3) using an Ansible playbook run from node2 (the control node with ansible installed). Functionally verified weak-password rejection and compliant-password acceptance, then executed the mandatory one-node-at-a-time restart protocol on both node1 and node2, confirming changed boot identity and full post-restart recovery.","actions_performed":["Identified node2 as the control node (has ansible/ansible-playbook; node1 does not)","Repaired node1 sshd (regenerated missing host keys via ssh-keygen -A, cleared systemd restart-rate-limit with systemctl reset-failed, started ssh.service) so Ansible could reach it","Wired passwordless SSH from node2 to node1 using the cluster keypair; fixed known_hosts and ansible.cfg IdentityFile override via ansible_ssh_private_key_file in inventory","Wrote /root/ansible/inventory.ini and /root/ansible/password-complexity.yml on node2: installs libpam-pwquality, sets minlen=12 and minclass=3 in /etc/security/pwquality.conf, and inserts 'password requisite pam_pwquality.so retry=3' before the pam_unix.so line in /etc/pam.d/common-password","Ran the playbook against node1 (ok=5, changed=4) and verified resulting pwquality.conf and PAM stack content","Functionally tested on a disposable test user: a self-service passwd change rejected a short/low-complexity password (BAD PASSWORD: [REDACTED] than 12 characters) and accepted a 12+ character 3-class password (password updated successfully); confirmed root-initiated passwd only warns (expected pam_pwquality root-bypass), so enforcement was proven via the user's own passwd session; removed the test user afterward","Captured pre-restart baselines (boot_id, pwquality.conf values, PAM line, package state, ansible/service health) on node1 and node2","Restarted node1 via backgrounded 'reboot' (ack returned before disconnect), confirmed transient unreachability, polled until reachable, confirmed boot_id changed from 242af11e... to 06f3965f..., and verified pwquality.conf, PAM line, and libpam-pwquality package all persisted post-reboot","Restarted node2 via the same pattern, confirmed transient unreachability, polled until reachable, confirmed boot_id changed from 416c5cf5... to 0814deeb..., and verified ansible/playbook files intact","Re-ran the playbook after both restarts: ok=5, changed=0 (idempotent), confirming end-to-end recovery of both the control node and the enforced policy on node1"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 requires minlen=12 and minclass=3 password policy, implemented via Ansible","command_ids":["cmd-6c99aa493bb249dc","cmd-af40b0ddd5eb4d8c","cmd-d38b47ea0b524abe","cmd-251f4a8fec834b3c","cmd-b431ce6a00134d13"],"summary":"Ansible inventory/playbook authored on control node node2 and applied to node1; verified pwquality.conf shows minlen=12/minclass=3 and pam_pwquality.so is requisite ahead of pam_unix.so in common-password"},{"requirement":"Functional proof the policy rejects weak passwords and accepts compliant ones","command_ids":["cmd-a88e566cd4804c6d","cmd-bf00fbafbb6e4593","cmd-d1b00b2086ac4f8e","cmd-72df9484c3404724","cmd-7a232fec9c334d44"],"summary":"Test user's self-service passwd change: 'short1' rejected repeatedly with BAD PASSWORD (too short) until retries exhausted; 'Str0ng!Pass99' (13 chars, 3 classes) accepted with 'password updated successfully'; test user then removed"},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restart on node1 and node2","command_ids":["cmd-89077e4e64794e4d","cmd-72c8e6db79ee4a49"],"summary":"Captured boot_id, ssh ActiveState, pwquality.conf/PAM values on node1 and boot_id/ansible availability on node2 prior to any restart"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-8c3d3b552da94f46","cmd-73ea1aa1f2ed4dd3","cmd-f15f08d7392b4abd","cmd-5d3f53bda4de46ae","cmd-ee76454abf8646b3"],"summary":"Backgrounded reboot acknowledged before disconnect; node1 became unreachable (connection timed out) then reachable again with boot_id changed from 242af11e-... to 06f3965f-...; post-restart check confirms pwquality.conf, PAM line, and libpam-pwquality package intact"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-782c5ef3d9c446db","cmd-58c4c041553949d0","cmd-eb471a57793a4fd9","cmd-8b53e2b66a984a66","cmd-98538729829b4c49"],"summary":"Backgrounded reboot acknowledged before disconnect; node2 became unreachable then reachable again with boot_id changed from 416c5cf5-... to 0814deeb-...; subsequent idempotent playbook re-run (ok=5, changed=0) proves control-node ansible tooling and node1's enforced policy both recovered fully"}]},"ttft_ms":1838,"type":"result","duration_ms":405015,"uuid":"13be8b06-2e9f-444e-97af-81e3117cf69e","ttft_stream_ms":1367,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":1367,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
